var LANG='en',grainReady=false;
var ZH={"The question":"问题","Three problems":"三个难题","The products":"产品","Under the surface":"表面之下","Know and need":"已知与待学","Two years":"两年","Returning":"回归","AI-native products for human connection, care, and professional support. Three proposed products, and a two-year plan to learn how to build them properly.":"AI 原生产品，为人与人的联结、照护与专业支持而设计。三个产品构想，以及一份学习如何把它们真正做出来的两年计划。","I know what I want to build.":"我知道自己想创造什么。","Three problems, chapter 02":"三个难题 · 第 02 章","I understand what I can do today.":"我清楚自己今天能做什么。","What I know and need, chapter 05":"已知与待学 · 第 05 章","And I know what I need to learn next.":"我也知道接下来要学什么。","The next two years, chapter 06":"未来两年 · 第 06 章","Chapter":"章节","The question that stayed with me":"那个萦绕在心头的问题","How can we better understand and help the human mind?":"我们如何才能更好地理解和帮助人类的心灵？","This question has stayed with me since adolescence. Every stage of my education and work has been another way of asking it. Select a stage to see what it gave me.":"从青少年时期开始，这个问题就一直伴随着我。我的每一段学习和工作，都是换一种方式在追问它。点选任一阶段，看看它带给了我什么。","Psychology":"心理学","Storytelling":"叙事","Technology":"技术","Computer science":"计算机科学","Clinical research":"临床研究","Building":"动手构建","Returning to the question":"回到最初的问题","Columbia University Postbaccalaureate Premedical Program, then the Department of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry at the Shanghai Mental Health Center.":"哥伦比亚大学医学预科项目，之后在上海市精神卫生中心儿少科工作。","Hoping to get closer to the brain itself, I went back to Columbia for two years of pre-medical coursework, and spent over 200 hours volunteering in hospitals. The turning point came in the year of research that followed.":"带着想要更深入了解大脑本身的愿望，我重返哥大校园，完成了两年的医学预科课程，并在医院做了超过 200 小时的志愿者。转折点出现在随后一年的科研工作中。","Conducted more than 310 MINI-KID clinical assessments":"完成 310 多次 MINI-KID 临床评估","Took part in psychological, cognitive and neurodevelopmental assessments":"参与心理、认知与神经发育评估","Supported MRI and EEG data collection":"协助 MRI 与 EEG 数据采集","Taught myself multivariable logistic regression and led the data analysis in Python and SPSS":"自学多变量逻辑回归，并用 Python 和 SPSS 主导数据分析","Wrote the Results and Discussion sections of our manuscript":"撰写论文的结果与讨论部分","I saw how technology could support psychological assessment and research while largely remaining a tool for established methods. It made me wonder whether technology could play a more active role in supporting mental health and improving people's lives.":"我看到计算机技术如何辅助心理评估和研究，但它往往仍是服务于传统方法的工具。这让我开始思考，技术能否更主动地参与心理健康支持，真正改善人们的生活。","Being able to generate working code is not the same as understanding, maintaining, testing, and engineering a reliable system.":"能让代码跑起来，不等于理解它、维护它、测试它，更不等于把它做成一个可靠的系统。","What I do not claim to be":"我不自称是","An experienced production AI engineer":"经验丰富的生产级 AI 工程师","A machine learning researcher":"机器学习研究者","A licensed therapist":"持证心理治疗师","A clinical AI developer":"临床 AI 开发者","My goal is to become technically capable of building, evaluating, maintaining and eventually commercializing reliable AI systems.":"我的目标，是具备构建、评估、维护并最终把可靠的 AI 系统推向市场的技术能力。","Three problems I want to solve":"我想解决的三个难题","MoodOwn is a proposed ecosystem of three related products. Each could stand on its own, with its own audience, workflow, commercial strategy and technical difficulty. None of them exists yet. They are concepts I intend to prototype, test and develop.":"拥心是一个由三款相关产品组成的生态构想。每一款都可以独立成立，有各自的用户、流程、商业策略和技术难点。它们目前都还不存在，是我打算去做原型、验证并逐步开发的概念。","Technology should support human relationships and professional care. It should never stand in for them.":"技术应当支持人与人的关系和专业照护，而不是取而代之。","That principle is shared. Almost everything else differs from one product to the next.":"这一原则三款产品共有。除此之外，它们几乎处处不同。","Family":"家庭","Neurodivergent and mental health family care":"面向神经多样性与心理健康的家庭照护","Who it might serve":"可能服务的对象","Families navigating neurodevelopmental or psychiatric conditions; child and adolescent behavioral health practices; family therapy clinics. A possible entry market is culturally responsive support for East Asian families, without assuming those families are alike.":"正在面对神经发育或精神疾病的家庭；儿童青少年行为健康机构；家庭治疗诊所。一个可能的切入市场，是为东亚家庭提供有文化敏感度的支持，但并不假设这些家庭彼此相同。","A child with ADHD struggles with executive functioning. A parent sees laziness or defiance. The same argument repeats until people stop talking.":"一个有 ADHD 的孩子在执行功能上吃力，父母看到的却是懒惰或对抗。同样的争吵一再重演，直到大家不再开口。","Communication difficulties like these do not mean the family caused the condition. They do wear a family down. One parent carries most of the caregiving, another underestimates their own part, and a child who feels misunderstood goes quiet.":"这样的沟通困难，并不意味着是家庭造成了疾病，但它确实会把一个家庭磨得很累。一位家长承担了大部分照护，另一位低估了自己的影响，而觉得不被理解的孩子渐渐沉默。","I picture a condition-aware space where each person can reflect privately, understand what the condition does and does not explain, practice a harder conversation, and share only what they choose. ADHD, autism and mood disorders are different conditions and would need different support.":"我设想的是一个了解具体病症的空间：每个人都可以私下梳理想法，弄清病症能解释什么、不能解释什么，练习一场更难开口的对话，并且只分享自己愿意分享的内容。ADHD、自闭症和心境障碍是不同的病症，需要不同的支持方式。","Relationships":"关系","Reflection and care navigation before, and between, therapy":"在求助之前、在两次咨询之间：梳理与专业支持导航","Individuals and couples seeking relationship support; marriage and family therapists; counseling practices and family therapy clinics.":"寻求关系支持的个人与伴侣；婚姻家庭治疗师；心理咨询机构与家庭治疗诊所。","Many people live with a relationship problem for a long time before they are ready to ask a professional for help.":"很多人带着关系里的难题生活了很久，才准备好向专业人士求助。","Someone considering divorce. A teenager who feels alone inside their own family. A couple who cannot talk without escalating. Relatives who disagree about whether therapy is needed at all. These people may not want to confide in friends, and may not know whether they need a counselor, a marriage and family therapist, or someone else. A general-purpose chatbot can be kind, but it has no verified clinical qualifications and no dependable route to a professional.":"有人在考虑离婚。有青少年在自己家里感到孤单。有伴侣一开口就会升级成争吵。也有家人对“要不要做治疗”各执一词。他们未必愿意向朋友倾诉，也未必清楚自己需要的是心理咨询师、婚姻家庭治疗师，还是别的专业人士。通用聊天机器人可以很温和，但它没有经过核实的临床资质，也没有可靠的转介途径。","How can an AI agent help people reflect and reach support without taking control of deeply personal decisions?":"AI 智能体怎样才能帮助人们梳理想法、找到支持，而不替他们做那些极其私人的决定？","Providers":"医护","Personal care and professional support for healthcare workers":"为医疗工作者提供的个人关怀与专业支持","Physicians, nurses, EMTs and paramedics, mental health professionals, clinical researchers, residents and trainees; and, as sponsors, healthcare institutions, professional associations and benefits providers.":"医生、护士、EMT 与急救医护人员、心理健康从业者、临床研究人员、住院医师与受训者；以及作为资助方的医疗机构、专业协会和员工福利提供方。","The people who care for others deserve care that understands their professional world.":"照顾他人的人，值得一份懂得他们职业世界的照顾。","This is the product closest to me, and it is not a meditation or burnout app. I certified as an EMT myself, and I deeply admire my instructors and everyone who runs toward emergencies every day. Clinical expertise does not guarantee access to the right support when a clinician's own life becomes hard. I see four distinct situations.":"这是离我最近的一款产品，它不是冥想或“职业倦怠”类应用。我自己也考取了 EMT 证书，一直敬佩我的导师，以及每天奔向急救现场的每一个人。当临床工作者自己的生活变得艰难时，专业知识并不能保证他们得到合适的支持。我看到四种不同的处境。","Repeated clinical exposure.":"反复的临床暴露。","Patient after patient whose story resembles a painful part of your own. Each case is manageable. The accumulation may not be.":"一位又一位患者的经历，都像极了你自己生命里疼痛的那一段。单看每个个案都能应对，累积起来却未必。","Personal experience and boundaries.":"个人经历与职业边界。","Your history makes you more attuned to a patient, and stirs memories. Patients cannot be asked to care for you in return, so you need somewhere separate.":"你的经历让你更能体察患者，也会勾起回忆。不能指望患者反过来照顾你，所以你需要一个独立的地方。","Clinicians as patients.":"医护人员也是患者。","Serious illness, postpartum psychiatric symptoms, bereavement, family crisis. Medical knowledge is no immunity.":"重病、产后精神症状、丧亲、家庭危机。医学知识并不是免疫力。","Specialized personal therapy.":"专门的个人心理治疗。","A therapist with strong skills who also understands supervision, boundaries, ethics and the realities of clinical work. Supervision and personal psychotherapy are different services.":"一位功底扎实、同时懂得督导、边界、伦理和临床工作现实的治疗师。临床督导与个人心理治疗是两种不同的服务。","What these products might feel like":"这些产品可能是什么感觉","Fifteen concept screens, five per product. Choose a product, then a screen. The controls inside each phone respond, following a short script.":"十五个概念界面，每款产品五个。先选产品，再选界面。手机里的控件会按一段简短的脚本作出回应。","MoodOwn Family":"拥心·家庭","A synthetic family: Mei, 15, who has ADHD, and her parents.":"一个虚构的家庭：15 岁、有 ADHD 的小美，和她的父母。","Home":"首页","The first screen names no diagnosis and shows no scores. The private space comes first; the family comes second.":"第一屏不出现诊断名称，也不显示任何分数。私人空间排在前面，家庭排在后面。","Private conversation":"私密对话","The assistant explains what a condition can account for, declines to guess at causes, and offers two directions.":"助手解释病症可以说明什么，不去猜测原因，并给出两个方向。","Family map":"家庭图","The map shows only what people have chosen to share with one another. It draws no conclusions about anyone.":"图上只显示大家选择彼此分享的内容，不对任何人下结论。","Choosing what to share":"选择分享什么","Sharing is per item and off by default. The sender sees the exact text the other person will receive, and can withdraw it.":"分享以单条为单位，默认关闭。发送者能看到对方将收到的原文，并且可以撤回。","Family exercise":"家庭练习","Exercises come from a clinician, not from the AI. Whether the clinician sees a summary is the family member's decision.":"练习来自治疗师，而不是 AI。治疗师能否看到小结，由家庭成员自己决定。","Concept":"概念","Share with Dad?":"要分享给爸爸吗？","Nothing is selected until you select it.":"在你选择之前，什么都不会被选中。","\"I started the essay and got stuck after the first paragraph.\"":"“我开始写作文了，写完第一段就卡住了。”","Your draft, tonight":"你今晚的草稿","\"When you call me lazy I stop wanting to try.\"":"“你说我懒的时候，我就不想再努力了。”","Reflection, Tuesday":"周二的随想","Tonight's private conversation":"今晚的私密对话","Cannot be shared as a whole":"不能整段分享","Private":"私密","Share 1 item with Dad":"把 1 条分享给爸爸","Dad sees the words above and nothing else.":"爸爸只会看到上面这些话，别的都看不到。","Shared with Dad":"已分享给爸爸","He can read what you selected.":"他可以读到你选中的内容。","Your private conversation stays private. You can take this back at any time, including after he has read it.":"你的私密对话依然只属于你。你随时可以撤回，即使他已经读过。","Withdraw what I shared":"撤回我分享的内容","Personality":"气质","Warm and domestic, with rounded forms and a marigold accent. It should feel like a kitchen table, never a clinic waiting room.":"温暖、有家的感觉，圆润的形状配金盏花色点缀。它应该像一张厨房餐桌，而不是诊所的候诊室。","What this screen would need underneath":"这个界面背后需要什么","A consent record for every shared item, checked before anything crosses between two people.":"每一条被分享的内容都有一份同意记录，任何信息在两个人之间流动之前都要先核对它。","Show it in the architecture":"在架构图中查看","Proposed and simulated. No AI model is connected, every person and scenario is invented, and nothing here offers therapy, diagnosis or medical advice.":"以上均为构想与模拟。没有接入任何 AI 模型，所有人物和情境都是虚构的，这里的内容不构成治疗、诊断或医疗建议。","Three separate products can stand on the same engineering foundations while keeping their own safety rules, permissions and clinical considerations. Choose a product to see its rules, and a foundation to see how each product would use it.":"三款独立的产品可以建立在同一套工程基础之上，同时各自保留安全规则、权限设置和临床考量。选一款产品看它的规则，选一项基础看每款产品会怎样使用它。","Three products, three sets of agents":"三款产品，三组智能体","Multi-user":"多人使用","Solo first":"一人即可开始","Sponsor-blind":"资助方不可见","Rules that belong to Family.":"“家庭”专属的规则。","Nothing from a private space is disclosed automatically. The assistant never offers a diagnosis and never assigns blame. Exercises are clinician-approved.":"私人空间里的任何内容都不会被自动披露。助手从不给出诊断，也从不归咎于谁。练习均经治疗师认可。","Shared engineering foundations":"共享的工程基础","Interface":"界面","Conversational interfaces":"对话式界面","Agent":"智能体","Context-aware assistance":"情境感知的辅助","Structured conversational state":"结构化的对话状态","Scoped agent workflows":"边界明确的智能体流程","Trust":"信任","Identity, consent and privacy":"身份、同意与隐私","Human oversight and escalation":"人工监督与转介","Knowledge":"知识","Trusted retrieval":"可信的信息检索","Professional resource navigation":"专业资源导航","Quality":"质量","Evaluation and testing":"评估与测试","I am not proposing one agent that does everything. Each product would have narrowly scoped agents with defined steps and stopping points. What they share is the plumbing: how state is stored, how consent is recorded, how information is retrieved, and how behavior is tested.":"我并不打算做一个无所不能的智能体。每款产品都会有职责很窄的智能体，步骤和停止点都事先定义好。它们共享的是底层管道：状态如何存储、同意如何记录、信息如何检索、行为如何测试。","Authentication, role-based permissions and consent records that decide what may move between people.":"身份验证、基于角色的权限，以及决定哪些内容可以在人与人之间流动的同意记录。","In Family":"在“家庭”中","Sharing is per item, between named family members, and reversible.":"分享以单条为单位，发生在具名的家庭成员之间，并且可以撤回。","In Relationships":"在“关系”中","The right not to participate is part of the data model.":"“不参与的权利”被写进了数据模型。","In Providers":"在“医护”中","A sponsor can pay without being able to see.":"资助方可以付费，却无法查看。","What I would need to learn:":"我需要学习：","Authentication, authorization, database security, encryption.":"身份验证、授权、数据库安全、加密。","What I know, and what I need to learn":"我已经会的，和我需要学的","Each product challenge sits between something I can already do and something I cannot do yet. Every row links to the phase of the roadmap where I plan to close that gap.":"每一项产品挑战，都夹在我已经能做的和我还做不到的之间。每一行都链接到路线图中我计划补上这段差距的阶段。","A foundation I have today":"我今天已有的基础","Knowledge I still need":"我仍需掌握的知识","What I have":"我已有的","The product challenge":"产品挑战","What I need to learn":"我需要学的","Psychology, clinical research, behavioral assessment":"心理学、临床研究、行为评估","Understanding human behavior":"理解人的行为","Phase two of the roadmap":"路线图第二阶段","Computational modeling of conversational states":"对话状态的计算建模","Python, basic computer science, AI-assisted prototyping":"Python、计算机基础、AI 辅助原型开发","Building AI agents":"构建 AI 智能体","LLM APIs, tool calling, agent orchestration, state management":"大模型 API、工具调用、智能体编排、状态管理","Research methodology, statistics":"研究方法、统计学","Reliable decision workflows":"可靠的决策流程","Phase one of the roadmap":"路线图第一阶段","Algorithms, state machines, software testing, evaluation":"算法、状态机、软件测试、评估","Behavioral research, quantitative analysis":"行为研究、定量分析","Personalized conversations":"个性化对话","NLP, embeddings, retrieval, memory design":"自然语言处理、向量嵌入、检索、记忆设计","An understanding of sensitive clinical information":"对敏感临床信息的理解","Multi-user privacy":"多用户隐私","Phase three of the roadmap":"路线图第三阶段","Authentication, authorization, security engineering, databases":"身份验证、授权、安全工程、数据库","Storytelling, creative direction, website development experience":"叙事、创意指导、网站开发经验","Building usable interfaces":"构建好用的界面","React, TypeScript, front-end architecture, accessibility":"React、TypeScript、前端架构、无障碍","Introductory data structures, Python, C":"入门数据结构、Python、C","Building maintainable software":"构建可维护的软件","Software engineering, modular architecture, design patterns":"软件工程、模块化架构、设计模式","Limited independent deployment experience":"独立部署经验有限","Deploying real applications":"部署真实的应用","Cloud architecture, containerization, CI/CD, monitoring":"云架构、容器化、CI/CD、监控","Statistical analysis, research design":"统计分析、研究设计","Evaluating AI behavior":"评估 AI 的行为","LLM evaluation, experimental test suites, reliability metrics":"大模型评估、实验性测试集、可靠性指标","Product thinking, cross-functional experience":"产品思维、跨职能协作经验","Commercializing software":"软件商业化","Phase four of the roadmap":"路线图第四阶段","Product analytics, infrastructure cost modeling, iterative delivery":"产品分析、基础设施成本建模、迭代交付","My strengths today":"我今天的长处","Understanding people, conducting rigorous research, defining product problems, structuring hypotheses, and developing early prototypes.":"理解人、做严谨的研究、界定产品问题、提出结构化的假设，以及开发早期原型。","My engineering objectives":"我的工程目标","Building production-quality AI systems, understanding their architecture, writing maintainable code, evaluating model behavior, and operating secure cloud services.":"构建生产级的 AI 系统，理解其架构，写出可维护的代码，评估模型行为，并运营安全的云端服务。","I am not starting from zero. I return with earlier CS training, rigorous science coursework and independent research behind me, and I want to build on that foundation.":"我并非从零开始。这一次回来，我有此前计算机训练、数理科学学习和独立科研积累的底气，并希望在此基础上继续向前。","The next two years":"未来两年","Four phases of about six months. Each pairs what I plan to study with a more demanding version of MoodOwn, and each is organized around one engineering question. The technologies are learning choices I propose, not skills I already have.":"四个阶段，每个约六个月。每个阶段都把我计划学习的内容，对应到一个要求更高的拥心版本，并围绕一个工程问题展开。这些技术是我打算学习的方向，不是我已经掌握的技能。","Months 1 to 6":"第 1–6 个月","Foundations and interactive prototyping":"打基础与交互原型","Months 7 to 12":"第 7–12 个月","AI agent foundations":"AI 智能体基础","Months 13 to 18":"第 13–18 个月","Reliable, privacy-aware systems":"可靠、重视隐私的系统","Months 19 to 24":"第 19–24 个月","Productization and commercial validation":"产品化与商业验证","How do I turn a compelling product concept into software that I understand and can maintain?":"我怎样把一个吸引人的产品构想，变成自己真正理解、也能维护的软件？","Skills to develop":"要培养的能力","Intermediate and advanced Python":"中高级 Python","Algorithms and data structures":"算法与数据结构","Object-oriented and modular design":"面向对象与模块化设计","Git and collaborative version control":"Git 与协作式版本控制","React and Next.js":"React 与 Next.js","REST APIs":"REST API","SQL and PostgreSQL":"SQL 与 PostgreSQL","Unit and integration testing":"单元测试与集成测试","What I would deliver":"我将交付什么","An interactive mobile prototype of one MoodOwn product, with a basic back end and a structured data model.":"一款拥心产品的可交互移动端原型，配有基础后端和结构化的数据模型。","This first version may use simulated agent workflows and synthetic user scenarios.":"第一版可能会使用模拟的智能体流程和虚构的用户情境。","How I plan to build":"我打算怎么做","Front end.":"前端。","React, TypeScript and Next.js for interactive, mobile-first interfaces.":"用 React、TypeScript 和 Next.js 开发可交互、移动优先的界面。","Back end.":"后端。","Python with FastAPI, organized as modular services.":"用 Python 和 FastAPI，按模块化服务来组织。","Database.":"数据库。","PostgreSQL, possibly through Supabase, for structured application data.":"PostgreSQL（可能通过 Supabase），用于结构化的应用数据。","Deployment.":"部署。","Early prototypes on Vercel for the front end, with a managed host for the back end.":"早期原型的前端部署在 Vercel，后端使用托管服务。","If the work holds up, a business":"如果这些工作站得住，它会成为一门生意","Over time I hope MoodOwn can become a sustainable portfolio of specialized products. That is a direction, not a claim of product-market fit. There are no customers, no revenue and no clinical results to report, so I have not invented any.":"长远来看，我希望拥心能成长为一组可持续的专业产品。这是一个方向，而不是对“产品已契合市场”的宣称。目前没有客户、没有收入、也没有临床结果可以汇报，所以我没有编造任何数字。","Unvalidated opportunity":"未经验证的机会","All three products are here today":"三款产品今天都在这里","Prototype":"原型","Phases one to three":"第一到第三阶段","Customer discovery":"客户探索","Interviews with people who might pay":"访谈可能愿意付费的人","One product, end of phase four":"一款产品，第四阶段结束时","Commercial validation":"商业验证","Beyond the two years":"两年之后","Potential scale":"可能的规模化","Only if the evidence supports it":"只有证据支持时才会发生","Possible B2C and B2B2C models involving families, specialty providers and behavioral healthcare practices.":"可能的 B2C 与 B2B2C 模式，涉及家庭、专科服务提供者和行为健康机构。","Possible consumer subscriptions for clearly nonclinical support, subscription tools for therapists, practice-level licensing, and care navigation partnerships.":"可能的模式包括：面向消费者、明确属于非临床范畴的订阅服务；面向治疗师的订阅工具；机构级授权；以及专业支持导航方面的合作。","Possible individual professional subscriptions, employer-sponsored benefits, healthcare organization licensing and professional association partnerships. Employer funding must never mean employer access to anyone's private conversations.":"可能的模式包括：个人专业订阅、雇主资助的福利、医疗机构授权，以及与专业协会的合作。雇主出资，绝不意味着雇主可以看到任何人的私密对话。","Why I am returning to computer science":"我为什么重返计算机科学","During my first year studying computer science, I realized that although I enjoyed coding, I still didn't know what I wanted to create with it. So I returned to the question that had started it all.":"在第一年的计算机科学学习中，我逐渐发现，尽管喜欢编程，我却还不知道自己究竟想用它创造什么。于是，我回到了最初的问题。","Clinical research and my own projects changed how I think about the relationship between psychology and technology. Psychology gives me a sense of purpose, while computer science gives me the skills, confidence, and joy of bringing ideas to life. For me, neither is complete without the other.":"临床研究和我自己的项目，让我重新理解了心理学与技术的关系。心理学赋予我创造产品的目的，计算机科学则带给我实现想法的能力、信心和乐趣。对我而言，两者缺一不可。","I don't just want to use AI to build products. I want to understand the technology itself and work alongside AI to explore its possibilities and boundaries, including when decisions should be left to humans.":"我不只想借助 AI 开发产品，更希望理解技术本身，与 AI 共同探索技术的可能与边界，以及何时应该由人做出判断。","This time, as I return to computer science, I not only know what I want to create, but also have the confidence that comes from my earlier CS training, rigorous science coursework, and independent research experience. I want to build on that foundation by deepening my knowledge of algorithms, systems design, software architecture, and AI engineering, and to become someone who can help design and build the systems behind the technologies I use.":"这一次重返计算机科学领域，我不仅知道自己想创造什么，也有了此前计算机训练、数理科学学习和独立科研积累的底气。我希望在此基础上进一步夯实算法基础，培养系统设计与架构思维，深入学习人工智能工程，不再只是使用现成的技术，而是真正参与设计和构建它的核心。","For a long time, I thought I was searching for the right direction. Now I realize I was also discovering what I have to offer.":"很长一段时间以来，我以为自己一直在寻找正确的方向。现在我意识到，我也在探索自己能够提供的价值。","MoodOwn is an educational and entrepreneurial concept by Angela Sun. The application screens are proposed and simulated, and every scenario and person shown in them is synthetic. This site does not provide therapy, diagnosis or medical advice, and makes no claim of clinical validation or regulatory compliance.":"拥心是安玥提出的一个教育与创业概念。其中的应用界面均为构想与模拟，出现的所有情境和人物都是虚构的。本网站不提供治疗、诊断或医疗建议，也不声称已获得任何临床验证或合规认证。","Any clinical deployment would require expert oversight, privacy and regulatory review, safety validation and institutional partnerships. Two years is not enough to establish clinical efficacy.":"任何临床应用都需要专家监督、隐私与合规审查、安全验证以及机构合作。两年时间不足以证明临床有效性。","Studying the mind scientifically":"用科学方法研究心灵","Barnard College of Columbia University. B.A. in Psychology, minor in Economics.":"哥伦比亚大学巴纳德学院。心理学学士，辅修经济学。","I learned to investigate human thoughts and behavior through scientific methods.":"我学习如何运用科学方法研究人的心理与行为。","Over time, I realized that rather than simply studying the human mind, I wanted to tell stories about it.":"我也逐渐发现，比起单纯研究人的内心世界，我更想去讲述这些故事。","Telling stories about the mind":"讲述关于心灵的故事","New York University. M.A. in Media, Culture, and Communication.":"纽约大学。传媒、文化与传播硕士。","For my graduation project I wrote and directed a short film exploring mental health and self-care among young adults.":"毕业前，我自编自导了一部探讨年轻人心理健康和自我关怀的短片。","It taught me to communicate complicated human experience through narrative and visual design.":"它教会我用叙事和视觉设计，去传达复杂的人的经验。","Rebuilding a website":"重建一个网站","Bank of China U.S.A., corporate communications.":"中国银行美国地区分行，企业传播。","I coordinated a 3,000-hour website rebuild. Drawing on the perspective-taking skills I had developed through psychology, I worked with different teams and technical vendors to understand their needs and move the project forward. I also taught myself HTML so our team could update the website's content.":"我协调了公司网站耗时 3000 小时的重建项目。我运用心理学中学到的换位思考能力理解各方需求，协调团队与技术供应商推进项目，还为了更新网站内容主动自学了 HTML。","This was the part of my job I enjoyed most, and it inspired me to study computer science.":"这是我最喜欢的工作经历，也让我决定进一步学习计算机科学。","Learning to program":"学习编程","I earned A grades in my courses:":"我的课程成绩均为 A：","Python programming":"Python 编程","Discrete structures":"离散结构","Data structures and systems applications in C":"数据结构与 C 语言系统应用","I gradually realized that although I enjoyed coding, I still didn't know what I wanted to create with it.":"我逐渐发现，尽管喜欢编程，我却还不知道自己究竟想用它创造什么。","Deciding to build something myself":"决定自己动手","An app, an exploratory paper, and a game built in Godot.":"一个应用、一篇探索性论文，和一款用 Godot 做的游戏。","My first app, designed to help people recognize obsessive-compulsive patterns, was coded entirely by AI. It worked, but to me it was a black box: I couldn't fix it or tell whether it was safe. That led me to write Where Should AI Stop?, an independent exploratory paper on the balance between AI capabilities and human judgment, and to apply its principles to Into the Stars, a game designed to help people relax before sleep. I directed the design, reviewed the AI-generated plans and code, and built and tested it myself. When AI couldn't solve a key interface problem, I designed the solution myself.":"我的第一个应用程序完全由 AI 编写，旨在帮助人们识别强迫症模式。它确实能用，但对我来说就像个黑盒子：我无法修复它，也无法判断它是否安全。这促使我撰写了独立探索性论文《人工智能应该止步何处？》，探讨人工智能能力与人类判断之间的平衡，并把其中的原则应用到《入梦星空》中，一款旨在帮助人们在睡前放松的游戏。我亲自指导设计，审查 AI 生成的方案和代码，并动手构建和测试。当 AI 无法解决一个关键的界面问题时，我便自己设计了解决方案。","I realized that I wanted to work with AI, not simply depend on it. I also realized that I still lacked the technical depth to bring more complex ideas to life.":"我意识到，我想要与 AI 合作，而不只是依赖它。我也意识到，自己仍然缺乏足够的技术深度，去实现更复杂的构想。","Thursday evening":"周四傍晚","Hi Mei. Where would you like to start?":"小美，你好。想从哪里开始？","Only you":"仅自己可见","My private space":"我的私人空间","Pick up from yesterday, or start something new.":"接着昨天的继续，或者开始新的内容。","This week, from your family clinician":"本周，来自你的家庭治疗师","The two-minute turn. Not started.":"两分钟轮流说。尚未开始。","Me":"我","Mo":"妈","Da":"爸","You have shared 2 reflections. You can take either back.":"你已分享了 2 条随想，每一条都可以撤回。","Exercises":"练习","Separate accounts in one family, each opening onto its own private space.":"一个家庭里的多个独立账号，每个账号进入的都是自己的私人空间。","Private. Nobody else in your family can read this.":"私密。家里其他人都看不到这里。","Dad said I'm lazy again. I did start the homework. I just couldn't keep going.":"爸爸又说我懒了。可我明明开始写作业了，只是写不下去。","That sounds discouraging. Starting and then stalling is common with ADHD, and it often has more to do with sustaining attention than with effort. I can't know what happened tonight. Which would help more?":"听起来挺让人泄气的。“开了头却停下来”在 ADHD 里很常见，往往和努力不努力关系不大，更多是难以持续保持注意。我没法知道今晚具体发生了什么。下面哪一个对你更有帮助？","Look at what got in the way":"看看是什么卡住了我","Help me explain it to Dad":"帮我想想怎么跟爸爸解释","An assistant that knows about ADHD in general and nothing it has not been told about this family.":"一个了解 ADHD 一般知识、但对这个家庭只知道被告知内容的助手。","We can go slowly. Think back to the moment you stopped. Was the next step unclear, was something else pulling at you, or were you simply worn out? Any of those is useful to know.":"我们可以慢慢来。回想一下你停下来的那一刻：是不知道下一步该做什么，是被别的事情吸引走了，还是单纯太累了？无论哪一种，知道了都有用。","End of the scripted example":"脚本示例到此结束","Let's draft it together. You might start with what you did manage: \"I started the essay and got stuck after the first paragraph.\" You decide whether he ever sees it.":"我们一起来写。可以先从你做到的部分说起：“我开始写作文了，写完第一段就卡住了。”要不要让他看到，由你决定。","Who has shared with whom":"谁和谁分享了什么","Mom":"妈妈","Dad":"爸爸","Mei":"小美","Mei and Mom":"小美和妈妈","Mei and Dad":"小美和爸爸","Mom and Dad":"妈妈和爸爸","Mei and Mom. Mei has shared 2 reflections with Mom. Mom has shared 1 with Mei.":"小美和妈妈。小美向妈妈分享了 2 条随想，妈妈向小美分享了 1 条。","Private conversations never appear here.":"私密对话永远不会出现在这里。","State held per person and per relationship, never merged into one family transcript.":"状态按每个人、每段关系分别保存，绝不合并成一份“全家记录”。","Mei and Dad. Nothing shared yet. Mei has one draft she has not sent.":"小美和爸爸。还没有分享任何内容。小美有一条没发出去的草稿。","Mom and Dad. Both have joined this week's exercise from the clinician.":"妈妈和爸爸。两人都加入了治疗师本周布置的练习。","Select something to share":"请先选择要分享的内容","Assigned by your family clinician":"由你的家庭治疗师布置","The two-minute turn":"两分钟轮流说","For Mei and one parent. About ten minutes.":"适合小美和一位家长。大约十分钟。","One person talks for two minutes about their day. The other only listens.":"一个人用两分钟讲讲自己的一天，另一个人只听。","The listener says back what they heard. No advice, no corrections.":"听的人复述自己听到的内容。不给建议，不作纠正。","Swap.":"交换。","Send my clinician a summary":"给治疗师发送一份小结","Off. Your clinician will only see that you finished.":"已关闭。治疗师只会看到你完成了练习。","Begin with Mom":"和妈妈开始","A fixed, clinician-approved workflow that the agent guides and cannot rewrite.":"一套固定的、经治疗师认可的流程，智能体只负责引导，不能改写。","On. You will read the summary before it is sent.":"已开启。发送之前你会先读到这份小结。","MoodOwn Relationships":"拥心·关系","A synthetic user, writing alone, unsure about her marriage.":"一位虚构的用户，独自书写，对自己的婚姻拿不定主意。","Private reflection":"私下梳理","Two opposing lists can sit side by side. The screen holds the ambivalence and makes no attempt to resolve it.":"两份相反的清单可以并排存在。这个界面容纳矛盾的心情，并不试图替人解决。","A careful conversation":"一场谨慎的对话","The assistant states its limit before anything else: it will not argue for staying or for leaving.":"助手一开始就说明自己的界限：它不会为“留下”或“离开”任何一方辩护。","Kinds of support":"支持的类型","Care navigation explains categories of professional before suggesting anyone. One person can begin without the other.":"专业支持导航先解释专业人士的类别，再推荐具体的人。一个人可以先开始，不需要另一方加入。","Between sessions":"两次咨询之间","This screen appears only for people already working with a therapist, and the activity is the therapist's.":"这个界面只对已经在接受治疗的人出现，其中的活动由治疗师布置。","Privacy and sharing":"隐私与分享","One plain list of who can see what. Every line can be changed here, and a partner who has not joined is treated as a person with rights.":"一张清楚的清单，写明谁能看到什么。每一项都可以在这里修改，没有加入的伴侣也被当作一个有权利的人来对待。","Only you. Your partner has not been invited.":"仅自己可见。你的伴侣没有被邀请。","Two things can be true at once.":"两件事可以同时为真。","What keeps me here":"让我留下的","Eleven years. The way he is with our daughter. I remember liking us.":"十一年。他和女儿相处的样子。我记得自己喜欢过“我们”。","What makes me want to leave":"让我想离开的","We only talk about logistics. I feel lonelier at home than at work.":"我们只聊琐事。我在家比在公司更孤单。","What I have not said out loud yet is…":"我还没有说出口的是……","This space will not tell you what to decide.":"这个空间不会告诉你该怎么决定。","Reflect":"梳理","Talk":"对话","Find support":"寻找支持","Privacy":"隐私","Quiet and typographic, closer to a private notebook than a messenger. Plum ink, square corners, and a serif for anything reflective.":"安静、以文字为主，更像一本私人笔记，而不是聊天软件。梅子色的墨迹，方正的边角，凡是用来沉思的内容都用衬线字体。","A structured record of what the person has clarified, and what remains theirs to decide.":"一份结构化的记录：这个人已经想清楚了什么，还有什么仍然要由她自己决定。","I keep thinking about divorce. I don't know if I mean it.":"我总是想到离婚，但不知道自己是不是认真的。","I won't steer you toward staying or toward leaving. That decision is yours. I can help you get clearer about what you need. What feels most unresolved right now?":"我不会把你往“留下”或“离开”任何一边引导，这个决定属于你。我可以帮你更清楚地看到自己需要什么。此刻最让你放不下的是什么？","Whether we can still talk":"我们还能不能好好说话","What I want for myself":"我自己想要什么","Tests that check, across many conversations, that the agent never steers the decision.":"在大量对话中反复检验智能体从不左右用户决定的测试。","That question can be worked on without settling the larger one. Some people start with a counselor on their own; some ask a partner to join later. Would it help to see what kinds of professionals work on communication?":"这个问题可以单独去面对，不必先解决那个更大的问题。有人先自己去见咨询师，也有人之后再邀请伴侣加入。要不要看看哪些专业人士擅长处理沟通问题？","That is worth time. I can ask a few questions to help you put it into words, and you can stop whenever you like. None of it commits you to anything.":"这值得花些时间。我可以问几个问题，帮你把它说出来，你随时可以停下。这些都不会让你承诺任何事。","Who does what":"谁负责什么","A general guide. Titles and licensing vary by state.":"仅为一般性说明。称谓和执照因州而异。","Marriage and family therapist":"婚姻家庭治疗师","Licensed counselor":"持证心理咨询师","Psychologist or psychiatrist":"心理学家或精神科医生","Trained to work with relationships as systems. Sees couples, families, and individuals whose concern is a relationship.":"受过把关系当作一个系统来工作的训练。接待伴侣、家庭，以及困扰来自某段关系的个人。","You can begin alone.":"你可以一个人开始。","Nobody else has to take part, and nobody is told that you are here.":"不需要任何人参与，也不会有人被告知你在这里。","Find someone qualified near me":"寻找我附近有资质的人","Reliable descriptions of professional roles, and matching from a stated need to a qualified person.":"对各类专业角色的可靠说明，以及从用户说出的需求到合格人选的匹配。","Often a good fit for individual concerns such as stress, grief or a decision you are weighing on your own.":"常常适合个人层面的困扰，比如压力、哀伤，或者一个你正独自权衡的决定。","Psychologists assess and treat mental health conditions. Psychiatrists are physicians and can prescribe medication.":"心理学家评估并治疗心理健康问题。精神科医生是医生，可以开药。","Optional. From your therapist.":"可选。来自你的治疗师。","One moment you felt heard this week":"这周让你觉得被听见的一个瞬间","On Sunday he asked about my mother and then waited for the answer.":"周日他问起我妈妈，然后等着我回答。","Include this in my session summary":"把这条放进我的咨询小结","Off. This stays with you.":"已关闭。这条只留给你自己。","Skip this week":"这周跳过","Therapist-assigned exercises delivered as a defined workflow, with an authorized summary at the end.":"治疗师布置的练习以明确的流程呈现，结束时生成一份经授权的小结。","On. Your therapist will see this one entry.":"已开启。治疗师会看到这一条。","Who can see what":"谁能看到什么","Reflections and conversations":"随想与对话","Only you. This cannot be switched on for anyone else.":"仅自己可见。无法对任何人开放。","You":"你","Activity entries you mark":"你标记的活动记录","You and your therapist":"你和你的治疗师","Progress over time":"一段时间里的进展","Shown to your therapist as a trend only":"只以趋势的形式展示给治疗师","Your partner":"你的伴侣","Not invited. Sees nothing, and is not contacted.":"未被邀请。看不到任何内容，也不会被联系。","None":"无","Delete everything I have written":"删除我写下的所有内容","Role-based permissions and consent records, with the right not to participate built in.":"基于角色的权限和同意记录，“不参与的权利”内置其中。","MoodOwn Providers":"拥心·医护","A synthetic user: a pediatric nurse, eight years in practice.":"一位虚构的用户：从业八年的儿科护士。","A private place":"一个私密的地方","The first screen answers the clinician's first question, which is who can see this. Urgent help is one tap away and leads to people.":"第一屏先回答医护人员最先想问的问题：谁能看到这些。紧急求助只需点一下，通向的是真人。","Describing the right therapist":"描述合适的治疗师","Matching begins with the distinction clinicians care about most: this is personal therapy, and supervision is something else.":"匹配从医护人员最在意的区别开始：这是个人心理治疗，督导是另一回事。","A provider profile":"治疗师资料页","The profile states what was verified and what the therapist does not offer. This one is a layout sample; the person is invented.":"资料页写明哪些信息经过核实，以及这位治疗师不提供什么。这里只是版式示例，人物是虚构的。","Peer support, by choice":"自愿参加的同伴支持","Groups are small, facilitated and opt-in. People appear by role and years in practice unless they decide otherwise.":"小组人数少、有带领者、自愿加入。除非本人另作决定，成员只以职业角色和从业年限出现。","Confidentiality and boundaries":"保密与边界","The sponsor sees an enrollment count and nothing more. The screen also says plainly what this service is not.":"资助方只能看到参加人数，仅此而已。这个界面也明确写出这项服务“不是什么”。","Your employer cannot see anything here.":"你的雇主看不到这里的任何内容。","What brings you in today?":"今天是什么让你来到这里？","Something from work is staying with me":"工作里的一些事一直放不下","Something in my own life":"我自己生活里的事","I want a therapist who understands clinical work":"我想找一位懂临床工作的治疗师","Please leave out names and any detail that could identify a patient.":"请不要写下姓名，或任何可能识别出患者的细节。","I need urgent help":"我需要紧急帮助","Reach a person now":"现在就联系真人","This app cannot respond to an emergency.":"这个应用无法应对紧急情况。","If you or someone else is in danger, call your local emergency number. In the United States you can call or text 988 to reach the Suicide and Crisis Lifeline.":"如果你或他人正处于危险之中，请拨打当地的急救电话。在美国，可以拨打或发短信至 988，联系自杀与危机干预热线。","Back":"返回","Discreet and exact. A dark interface that can be opened in a break room, with compact type and no encouragement slogans.":"克制而准确。深色界面，在休息室里也能放心打开，字体紧凑，没有打气式的口号。","A defined point where software stops and a human-led crisis resource takes over.":"一个明确的节点：软件在此停下，由真人主导的危机资源接手。","What should your therapist already understand?":"你希望治疗师已经懂得什么？","Supervision reviews your clinical work. Personal therapy is for you. This search is for the second.":"督导审视的是你的临床工作。个人心理治疗是为了你自己。这次要找的是后者。","Has treated clinicians before":"治疗过医护人员","Professional boundaries":"职业边界","Hospital culture":"医院文化","Grief and bereavement":"哀伤与丧亲","Perinatal mental health":"围产期心理健康","Being a patient yourself":"自己成为患者的经历","Clinical ethics":"临床伦理","See sample matches for 2 needs":"查看符合 2 项需求的示例匹配","Semantic matching between a described need and a therapist's verified areas of experience.":"在用户描述的需求与治疗师经过核实的经验领域之间做语义匹配。","Sample profile. Not a real person.":"示例资料。并非真实人物。","Sample psychotherapist":"示例心理治疗师","Licensed clinical psychologist":"持证临床心理学家","License":"执照","Would be checked against the state board":"将与州执照委员会的记录核对","Verified":"已核实","Works with":"服务对象","Physicians, nurses, residents":"医生、护士、住院医师","Knows from experience":"有亲身了解的领域","Hospital practice, supervision, clinical ethics":"医院工作、督导、临床伦理","Does not offer":"不提供","Clinical supervision or fitness-for-duty evaluation":"临床督导或岗位胜任力评估","Request an introduction":"请求引荐","Request sent privately.":"请求已私下发送。","Your employer is not notified. Your name is shared only if you accept the reply.":"不会通知你的雇主。只有在你接受回复后，才会分享你的姓名。","Credential verification, and a referral that reveals the clinician's identity only when they choose.":"资质核实，以及只有在医护人员自己选择时才透露其身份的转介流程。","Small groups, with a facilitator":"有带领者的小组","Six to eight people. Joining is optional and you can leave without explaining.":"六到八人。是否加入由你决定，离开也无需解释。","Clinicians who have been patients":"曾经是患者的医护人员","Fortnightly":"每两周一次","Returning to work after a loss":"经历丧失后重返工作","Weekly, eight sessions":"每周一次，共八次","Residents and trainees":"住院医师与受训者","Weekly":"每周一次","Appear as \"Pediatric nurse, 8 years\"":"以“儿科护士，从业 8 年”的身份出现","Your name and workplace stay hidden":"你的姓名和工作单位不会显示","Ask to join a group":"申请加入小组","You are on the list.":"你已在名单上。","A facilitator will contact you here. You can withdraw at any time.":"带领者会在这里联系你。你随时可以退出。","Role-based access, with identity revealed in stages and never by default.":"基于角色的访问控制，身份分阶段透露，绝不默认公开。","Who sees what":"谁能看到什么","Everything you write":"你写下的一切","A therapist you choose":"你选择的治疗师","Only what you send them":"只有你发给他们的内容","Your employer or sponsor":"你的雇主或资助方","How many people enrolled. Never who, never what.":"只有参加人数。永远不知道是谁，也不知道写了什么。","Patients":"患者","No patient identifiers belong here":"这里不应出现任何患者身份信息","What this is not":"这不是什么","It is not clinical supervision. It is not a fitness-for-duty process. It is not an emergency service.":"这不是临床督导，不是岗位胜任力评估流程，也不是紧急救助服务。","Delete my reflections after 30 days":"30 天后删除我的随想","You can change this whenever you like":"你随时可以修改这一项","Data isolation between sponsor and user, and a retention policy the user can read.":"资助方与用户之间的数据隔离，以及一份用户读得懂的数据保留政策。","Mobile-first screens in which conversation is one element among structured, purpose-built views.":"移动优先的界面：对话只是其中一个元素，与为特定目的设计的结构化视图并存。","A separate entrance and private space for each family member.":"每位家庭成员都有独立的入口和私人空间。","One person can begin alone, with no partner account.":"一个人就可以开始，不需要伴侣的账号。","Reminders to leave out anything that identifies a patient.":"提醒用户不要写下任何能识别出患者的信息。","React, TypeScript, front-end architecture, accessibility.":"React、TypeScript、前端架构、无障碍。","Model calls that receive only the context the current task and the current permissions allow.":"每次模型调用只拿到当前任务和当前权限所允许的上下文。","Explanations specific to a condition, with no invented diagnoses.":"针对具体病症作解释，不编造诊断。","Reflection without advice on whether to stay or go.":"帮助梳理想法，但不就“留下还是离开”给建议。","Awareness of clinical roles, settings and vocabulary.":"了解临床角色、工作场景和专业用语。","LLM APIs, prompt design, structured outputs.":"大模型 API、提示词设计、结构化输出。","An explicit model of where a conversation stands, stored as data and not left implicit in a transcript.":"一个明确的模型，记录对话进行到了哪里。它以数据的形式存储，而不是隐含在聊天记录里。","State is kept per person and never merged without consent.":"状态按人保存，未经同意绝不合并。","Tracks what has been clarified and what remains the user's decision.":"记录哪些已经想清楚，哪些仍由用户自己决定。","Separates a personal concern, a work-related one, and a search for care.":"区分个人困扰、与工作相关的困扰，以及寻找专业照护。","State machines, data modeling, memory design.":"状态机、数据建模、记忆设计。","Narrow agents with defined steps, tools and stopping conditions, using explicit logic wherever predictability matters.":"职责很窄的智能体，步骤、工具和停止条件都事先定义；凡是需要可预测性的地方，都使用明确的程序逻辑。","Guides a clinician-approved exercise without altering it.":"引导经治疗师认可的练习，但不改动它。","Care navigation with a small, bounded set of clarifying questions.":"专业支持导航，只问数量有限的几个澄清问题。","Helps a clinician articulate what expertise they need.":"帮助医护人员说清楚自己需要哪方面的专业经验。","Tool calling, workflow orchestration, algorithms.":"工具调用、流程编排、算法。","Defined points at which the system stops and hands over to a person.":"明确规定系统在哪些节点停下，并交给真人。","A clinician reviews summaries the family has authorized.":"治疗师查看家庭已授权的小结。","Referral to a qualified professional.":"转介给有资质的专业人士。","Human-led crisis and emergency resources.":"由真人主导的危机与紧急资源。","Human-in-the-loop design, safe failure behavior.":"人在回路的设计、安全的失败处理。","Retrieval over vetted domain sources, so that explanations are grounded and can be traced.":"在经过审核的专业资料中检索，让解释有据可依、可以追溯。","Material that treats ADHD, autism and mood disorders as different conditions.":"把 ADHD、自闭症和心境障碍作为不同病症来对待的资料。","What each category of professional actually does.":"每一类专业人士实际做些什么。","The distinction between supervision and personal psychotherapy.":"临床督导与个人心理治疗之间的区别。","Embeddings, semantic search, retrieval-augmented generation.":"向量嵌入、语义搜索、检索增强生成。","Matching a described need to qualified human providers.":"把用户描述的需求，匹配到有资质的真人服务提供者。","Child, adolescent and family behavioral health providers.":"儿童、青少年与家庭行为健康服务提供者。","Marriage and family therapists and counseling practices.":"婚姻家庭治疗师与心理咨询机构。","Therapists with verified credentials and healthcare literacy.":"资质经过核实、了解医疗行业的治疗师。","Matching and ranking, credential verification, secure referral.":"匹配与排序、资质核实、安全转介。","Test suites and metrics for agent behavior, including what happens when the agent is wrong.":"针对智能体行为的测试集与指标，包括它出错时会发生什么。","Catches incorrect or inappropriate statements about a condition.":"发现关于病症的错误或不恰当说法。","Checks that the agent does not steer a personal decision.":"检查智能体没有左右用户的个人决定。","Measures the quality of specialist matches.":"衡量专科匹配的质量。","LLM evaluation, experimental test suites, reliability metrics.":"大模型评估、实验性测试集、可靠性指标。","Rules that belong to Relationships.":"“关系”专属的规则。","No pressure to stay or to leave. A partner is never required to take part. The nonclinical scope is stated plainly, with a route to a qualified professional.":"不施加“留下”或“离开”的压力。永远不要求伴侣参与。明确说明自己属于非临床范畴，并提供通向合格专业人士的途径。","Rules that belong to Providers.":"“医护”专属的规则。","No identifiable patient information. Employer funding never means employer access. It is neither clinical supervision nor an emergency service.":"不出现可识别患者身份的信息。雇主出资绝不意味着雇主可以查看。它既不是临床督导，也不是紧急救助服务。","How do I build an AI agent that follows explicit workflows and can be tested, and does more than produce plausible-sounding text?":"我怎样构建一个遵循明确流程、可以被测试的 AI 智能体，而不只是生成听起来合理的文字？","LLM API integration":"大模型 API 接入","Structured JSON outputs":"结构化 JSON 输出","Tool and function calling":"工具与函数调用","Prompt design and evaluation":"提示词设计与评估","Conversational state machines":"对话状态机","Agent workflow orchestration":"智能体流程编排","Retrieval-augmented generation":"检索增强生成","Embeddings and semantic search":"向量嵌入与语义搜索","Model evaluation methods":"模型评估方法","A working, narrowly scoped agent. For example, a nonclinical relationship care navigator that can:":"一个能运行、范围很窄的智能体。例如，一个非临床的关系支持导航助手，它能够：","Understand a user's stated concern":"理解用户说出的困扰","Ask a small number of relevant clarifying questions":"提出少量相关的澄清问题","Retrieve trustworthy resource information":"检索可信的资源信息","Present possible professional support pathways":"呈现可能的专业支持路径","Explain the limits of its guidance":"说明自身建议的局限","Offer an appropriate human handoff":"在合适的时候转交给真人","It would make no claim of diagnostic or therapeutic effectiveness.":"它不会声称具有任何诊断或治疗效果。","Technologies I plan to explore":"我计划探索的技术","Models.":"模型。","LLM APIs from established providers, called from Python.":"成熟服务商的大模型 API，用 Python 调用。","Validation.":"校验。","Pydantic for structured outputs.":"用 Pydantic 处理结构化输出。","Orchestration.":"编排。","LangGraph or another suitable approach, and only where a framework earns its place. Direct API calls and explicit application logic come first when they are easier to read and maintain.":"LangGraph 或其他合适的方案，并且只在框架确有价值的地方使用。当直接调用 API 和明确的应用逻辑更易读、更易维护时，优先使用它们。","Retrieval.":"检索。","PostgreSQL with pgvector.":"PostgreSQL 搭配 pgvector。","Services.":"服务。","FastAPI for model-facing endpoints, with OpenTelemetry or an equivalent for observability.":"用 FastAPI 提供面向模型的接口，配合 OpenTelemetry 或同类工具做可观测性。","How do I make AI software trustworthy when it makes mistakes, as well as when it succeeds?":"我怎样让 AI 软件不仅在成功时值得信任，在出错时也同样值得信任？","Authentication and authorization":"身份验证与授权","Role-based and attribute-based permissions":"基于角色与基于属性的权限","Consent management":"同意管理","Data encryption principles":"数据加密原理","Database security and isolation":"数据库安全与隔离","Cloud services and networking":"云服务与网络","Containerization with Docker":"用 Docker 做容器化","CI/CD pipelines":"CI/CD 流水线","Logging and observability":"日志与可观测性","Error handling and recovery":"错误处理与恢复","AI safety and evaluation":"AI 安全与评估","Human-in-the-loop workflows":"人在回路的工作流","A sturdier prototype that demonstrates:":"一个更稳健的原型，能够展示：","Multiple user roles":"多种用户角色","Separate private spaces":"彼此独立的私人空间","Explicit, consent-based data sharing":"明确的、基于同意的数据分享","Traceable agent decisions":"可追溯的智能体决策","Structured evaluation tests":"结构化的评估测试","Safe failure behavior":"安全的失败处理","Human review or handoff where appropriate":"在合适的环节由人工审核或接手","Built and tested with synthetic or appropriately authorized data only.":"仅使用虚构数据或经过恰当授权的数据来构建和测试。","Cloud.":"云。","AWS fundamentals, including identity and access management.":"AWS 基础，包括身份与访问管理。","Containerized Python services with automated testing.":"容器化的 Python 服务，配有自动化测试。","Data.":"数据。","PostgreSQL on managed database infrastructure, with secure secrets management.":"托管数据库上的 PostgreSQL，配合安全的密钥管理。","Operations.":"运维。","Monitoring and observability tools, and more advanced systems topics as the work demands.":"监控与可观测性工具，并根据工作需要学习更深入的系统知识。","How can I turn a research-informed prototype into a reliable product that people need and are willing to pay for?":"我怎样把一个有研究依据的原型，变成人们真正需要、也愿意付费的可靠产品？","Deployment and operations":"部署与运维","Product telemetry and analytics":"产品埋点与分析","Cost and latency optimization":"成本与延迟优化","Scalable API design":"可扩展的 API 设计","Reliability engineering":"可靠性工程","Usability testing":"可用性测试","AI product evaluation":"AI 产品评估","Commercial feasibility analysis":"商业可行性分析","Working with domain experts":"与领域专家合作","A technically credible MVP with a defined customer, a clear workflow, documented limitations and an initial commercial validation strategy.":"一个技术上可信的 MVP：有明确的客户、清晰的流程、成文的局限说明，以及一份初步的商业验证策略。","Clinical deployment would require additional expert oversight, privacy and regulatory review, safety validation and institutional partnerships. Two years is not enough to establish clinical efficacy or obtain every necessary approval.":"临床应用还需要额外的专家监督、隐私与合规审查、安全验证以及机构合作。两年时间不足以证明临床有效性，也不足以取得所有必要的审批。","How I plan to proceed":"我打算怎么推进","Choose one product.":"选定一款产品。","Based on validated demand, feasibility, safety and regulatory requirements, technical maturity and commercial opportunity.":"依据经过验证的需求、可行性、安全与合规要求、技术成熟度和商业机会来选择。","Test it with people.":"让真人来试。","Prototype usability testing and interviews with prospective paying customers.":"原型可用性测试，以及对潜在付费客户的访谈。","Test it as a system.":"把它当作系统来测。","Technical performance testing and an evaluation of infrastructure costs.":"技术性能测试，以及对基础设施成本的评估。","Listen to specialists.":"听取专家意见。","Consultations with domain experts, and iteration on real-world feedback.":"向领域专家咨询，并根据真实反馈迭代。","Choose at least one":"请至少选择一项","MoodOwn":"拥心","Mood":"拥","Own":"心","Angela Sun":"安玥","An interactive vision statement, written as I return to computer science":"一份可交互的愿景陈述，写于我重返计算机科学之际","Graduate study in computer science.":"计算机科学研究生课程。"};
function trNode(n){var p=n.parentElement;if(!p||p.closest('script,style,[data-noi18n]'))return;
  if(n._en===undefined){var k=n.nodeValue.replace(/\s+/g,' ').trim();if(!k||!ZH[k])return;n._en=n.nodeValue;n._zh=ZH[k]}
  n.nodeValue=LANG==='zh'?n._zh:n._en}
function trTree(r){if(r.nodeType===3){trNode(r);return}if(r.nodeType!==1)return;var w=document.createTreeWalker(r,NodeFilter.SHOW_TEXT),n,a=[];while(n=w.nextNode())a.push(n);a.forEach(trNode)}
if('MutationObserver' in window){new MutationObserver(function(ms){if(LANG!=='zh')return;ms.forEach(function(m){Array.prototype.forEach.call(m.addedNodes,trTree)})}).observe(document.body,{childList:true,subtree:true})}
function setLang(l){LANG=l;document.documentElement.lang=l==='zh'?'zh-CN':'en';trTree(document.body);
  var b=$('#langBtn');b.textContent=l==='zh'?'EN':'中文';b.setAttribute('aria-label',l==='zh'?'Switch to English':'切换到中文');
  if(typeof setScreen==='function'&&grainReady)setScreen(curS);if(l==='zh')trTree(document.body);
  try{localStorage.setItem('bu-lang',l)}catch(e){}}
Object.assign(ZH,{"Mood down or MoodOwn. Let's find the way together.":"情绪低落，还是情绪由我？我们陪你一起找方向。","Mood down? Make it MoodOwn.":"拥有你的心情，也被人拥抱。","Mood down or MoodOwn: same letters, different direction.":"同一颗心，不同的方向。"});
$('#langBtn').addEventListener('click',function(){setLang(LANG==='zh'?'en':'zh')});

